      "credit": "DSC09026 - 1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan",
      "source": "DSC09026 - 1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan (36823715580)",
      "description": "1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan\n1924 is the year that Case was abandoned.\nFour Cylinder, Thirty-five horsepower.\nAll steel body - a specialty of the Dodge Brothers and one of the firsts for its time. An affordable everyman’s car, Dodge still managed a few upscale touches: solid wheels, running board steps, a taller grille design that was new for 1924. In addition, this one even wears double bumpers that were an option. And in the rear: roll down windows, heat vent and sunshades.\n\n\nThe Carriage Room and Garage features vintage automobiles from the early 1900s as well as some old carriages.",
